/* @catalog — generated by `npm run catalog:generate`; do not edit by hand.
 * Internal
 *   Classes: Storage
 *   Functions: mutation, code, stored, sha, pngOf, wav, taggedWav, project, audio, upload, choice, asset,
 *              fresh, distinctAll, named, approve, fixture, embeddedOf, completedWithCandidates
 *   Constants: actor, other, fixtureAdmin, PRIVATE
 *   Variables: harness, sample
 * Tests
 *   - each confirmed audio upload records the digest of the image it carries at admission; none or an invalid image records null, and a replay keeps it
 *   - the image every confirmed file shares is chosen automatically, takes no receipt, and is re-evaluated as the file set changes
 *   - an explicit choice, including No cover, wins and stays explicit while files change; removing the chosen image leaves explicit No cover
 *   - an Album decision of skip deselects the automatic cover, and create selects it again
 *   - a shared image whose staging outcome is unknown is chosen once reconciliation confirms it under the automatic intent
 *   - a shared image the staging bound kept out selects nothing, while its evidence is still recorded
 *   - approving the shown automatic cover freezes it and keeps the choice automatic; showing No cover is explicit; an append freezes none
 *   - completion cleans every unselected automatic candidate through the cleanup lifecycle, keeping the selected cover, the audio and a manual cover
 *   - a failed automatic cleanup needs attention, and any current administrator retries it with the original intent
 *   - a lost DELETE response leaves the automatic cleanup failed with the object gone, and the same intent completes it
 *   - after the publisher loses the role, automatic cleanup needs attention and another current administrator completes it
 *   - imports completed before automatic covers are swept once, cleaning their unselected per-file candidates
 *   - a candidate still in its transfer window waits for it to settle
 *   - a pass stopped between deletions resumes the same intents once its lease expires
 *   - no automatic cleanup runs for an active or cancelled publication, a newer-format project or a catalog review
 *   - an approval showing the automatic cover but carrying the manual cover saves that explicit choice, and completion cleans the automatic candidate
 *   - replacing the only file with one carrying another image cleans the old candidate first and selects the new image
 *   - a replaced candidate whose image another file still carries is kept, and the last file replaced stages the new shared image
 *   - a failed cleanup of a replaced candidate needs attention and leaves the new image unstaged, and a stopped one is resumed by the next staging
 *   - an approval whose own decisions create the Album the saved project skipped saves the No cover it showed, and completion cleans the candidate
 *   - a legacy import completed with no stored cover choice and no published cover shows none and cleans every per-file duplicate
 *   - a shared image whose staging failed selects nothing, and completion cleans the failed candidate record without a DELETE
 *   - an approval this release cannot read is never cleaned here, and the sweep looks at it again a day later
 *   - a cleanup intent another receipt already holds is never reused, so that candidate is kept
 *   - the publication worker sweeps a completed import on a tick that publishes nothing
 * @end-catalog */

/**
 * Automatic embedded covers end to end: admission evidence, the derived choice, approval, and the cleanup completion runs through
 * the ordinary staged cleanup lifecycle (adminImportCoverAutomation.ts, adminImportCoverCleanup.ts). Synthetic data only.
 */
